---
description: Permanent plaintiff-first stipulation drafting and review policy across all portfolio matters.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow `internal/docs/STIPULATION_DEFENSE.md` when the work is actually a stipulation or defense agreement — extra time, a stay, a waiver, expanded relief, or his signature on their paper. Use discretion: be firm on those asks; treat authenticity, name corrections he already wants, and court-asked magistrate-settlement yes as ordinary. Do not import that voice into status reports, oppositions, complaints, or other ordinary Plaintiff papers. When it applies: draft the most plaintiff-favorable supported terms; maintain or shorten defense deadlines where advantageous while preserving Plaintiff's preparation time. Include a deadline comparison, concession audit, and plaintiff-favorable draft. Identify concrete Plaintiff benefit for any exception. Do not silently waive rights, expand defense options, authorize signatures, or treat proposed dates as operative.
